# sbc -- the Bluetooth A2DP codec, and the difference between "bluetooth pairs"
# and "bluetooth plays sound".
#
# This package has exactly one consumer: pipewire's bluez5 SPA plugin, which
# builds spa-codec-bluez5-sbc and spa-codec-bluez5-faststream against libsbc
# UNCONDITIONALLY -- neither is behind a `found()` guard in
# spa/plugins/bluez5/meson.build. SBC is the codec every A2DP sink is required
# to implement, so it is the one that makes the profile work at all; every other
# codec pipewire can build is an improvement on it, never a substitute.
#
# Packaged AHEAD of the bluez5 re-enable rather than with it, because the
# re-enable is blocked on bluez (another chain) and this is not. See the
# follow-up note in pkgs/pipewire/pkg.env.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
#
# The book records an md5 and this file records a sha256, so the two were
# checked against the same bytes: md5 46e29f9c2fbd07c417194e5da60b6d48, which is
# the book's, and the sha256 below.
SRC_URL=https://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/bluetooth/sbc-2.1.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=426633cabd7c798236443516dfa8335b47e004b0ef37ff107e0c7ead3299fcc2
SRC_DIR=sbc-2.1

# --disable-tester IS REQUIRED TO BUILD AT ALL, and the dependency page says the
# opposite. BLFS lists libsndfile as "optional, needed only if you want to
# enable the SBC tester functionality", which reads as something configure
# detects and skips. It is not. configure.ac:
#
#     if (test "${enable_tester}" != "no"); then
#             PKG_CHECK_MODULES(SNDFILE, sndfile, dummy=yes,
#                                     AC_MSG_ERROR(sndfile library is required))
#
# enable_tester is UNSET by default, and "" != "no" is true, so the default path
# is the one that hard-errors. libsndfile is not packaged here, so without this
# flag the recipe stops at configure on a dependency described as optional.
#
# The part that makes it worth writing down rather than just passing: sbctester
# is `noinst_PROGRAMS` in Makefile.am. It is never installed. So the default
# build takes a hard dependency on a library nobody packages in order to produce
# a binary that does not ship. Read the default, not the description.
#
# --disable-tools is a real feature cut and is stated as one. It drops
# sbcinfo/sbcdec/sbcenc, three command-line utilities that need no dependency
# beyond what libsbc already needs and that nothing in this tree consumes: no
# recipe calls find_program for any of them, and the desktop reaches SBC through
# pipewire's codec plugin rather than through a shell. install.sh asserts they
# are ABSENT rather than trusting the flag, which is the same reasoning
# alsa-lib's assertions use -- a flag can be misspelled or renamed upstream, a
# file either exists or does not.
#
# Re-enabling them is a subversion bump AND an entry in tools/program-index.tsv
# for each binary, so it is a deliberate change rather than a free one.
#
# NOT PASSED, and each for a reason:
#   --enable-high-precision   changes the encoder's arithmetic and therefore its
#                             output. Off by default, off in BLFS, and nothing
#                             here asks for it. Left at the upstream default
#                             deliberately: this is a codec, and "sounds
#                             different from every other distribution's SBC" is
#                             not a property to acquire by accident.
#   --enable-pie              build.sh owns the tree-wide compiler flags; a
#                             recipe setting its own would be a second source of
#                             truth about hardening.
#
# There is no ambient-detection flag left to pin. sbc's configure probes for
# nothing except sndfile, which the tester flag above removes entirely, so this
# package builds the same artefact in any image -- which is not something to
# assume, and is why the option surface was read rather than sampled.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static --disable-tester --disable-tools"
